{
    "background_story": "Artemis was a majestic thoroughbred with a shiny black coat and a spirited personality. She was named after the Greek goddess of the hunt, and her owner, a renowned chef, thought it fitting to pair her name with a nod to his culinary expertise. Sirloin, the chef's prized restaurant, was where Artemis would often accompany her owner on deliveries, earning her the nickname 'Sirloin's Star'. As the restaurant's mascot, Artemis would proudly prance alongside the chef, her mane braided with a sprig of rosemary, as they delivered the finest cuts of meat to the city's top eateries. Artemis loved the attention, and her owner loved her loyalty - she was always by his side, whether in the kitchen or on the track, where she would gallop with the wind in her mane, as free as the huntress she was named after.",
